From: sathish123m <sathish085580@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:25:49 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] 9934: Fix help builds failing when a path contains a module
 name

getModulePathFromJar() in gradle/helpProject.gradle locates a module's
directory by searching the classpath jar path for the module name with
String.indexOf(). That returns the first occurrence of the name anywhere
in the path, so a checkout under a folder containing a module name--for
example "Projects", "IdeaProjects" or "Default Project"--truncates the
path at that folder.

The affected module's src/main/resources is then missing from the
help-builder classpath and its theme files are not tracked as task inputs.
Since the Project module holds many shared icons (plugin.png,
view-refresh.png, ...), the theme files referencing them fail to parse and
help validation reports invalid image links, failing :Debugger:buildHelpFiles
on a clean build.

Use the position of the module name from the regex match instead of a
string search.
---
 gradle/helpProject.gradle | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gradle/helpProject.gradle b/gradle/helpProject.gradle
index 57ab3fd842..6a984ba69c 100644
--- a/gradle/helpProject.gradle
+++ b/gradle/helpProject.gradle
@@ -138,7 +138,9 @@ def getModulePathFromJar(File file) {
 	}
 	
 	def moduleName = matcher.group(1);
-	def index = forwardSlashedPath.indexOf(moduleName) + moduleName.length()
+	// Use the match position, as the module name may also appear earlier in the path
+	// (e.g., in a parent workspace directory name)
+	def index = matcher.start(1) + moduleName.length()
 	return forwardSlashedPath.substring(0, index)
 }
 
